<article class="env-lemma" id="03GU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03GU">Lemma <span data-tag="03GU">29.57.3</span>.</a> Let $f : Y \to X$ be a morphism of schemes. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X$ and $Y$ are affine, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is quasi-finite. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then there exists a diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Y \ar[rd]_ f \ar[rr]_ j &  &  Z \ar[ld]^\pi \\  &  X &  }  \]
</div>
  <p> with $Z$ affine, $\pi $ finite and $j$ an open immersion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00QB" data-tag="00QB">10.123.14</a> reformulated in the language of schemes. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>